================================================================================
OPEN-CORE LICENSING MODEL
================================================================================

This repository uses a strict two-tier open-core model. Each tier has its own
self-contained, unambiguous licence file. This file is an index; the
tier-specific files are the authoritative legal texts.

There is intentionally no "catch-all" proprietary clause in this index file.
Every module is governed solely by its designated licence below.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIER 1 — COMMUNITY  (Apache License 2.0 + Commons Clause)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Modules:
  - exeris-kernel-spi
  - exeris-kernel-core
  - exeris-kernel-community
  - exeris-kernel-tck

Licence file: LICENSE-COMMUNITY (at the root of this repository)
Each of the above modules is governed by LICENSE-COMMUNITY; they reference the
single copy at the root of this repository.

Summary of rights granted:
  * Use in any project, including commercial production deployments — YES.
  * Modify and create derivative works — YES.
  * Redistribute (source or binary) — YES, with attribution and licence notice.
  * Fork and publish your own implementation of the SPI — YES, this is the
    intended ecosystem behaviour. Writing a competing QUIC implementation on
    the published SPI is explicitly permitted and encouraged.
  * Sell the Community modules themselves as a standalone hosted runtime,
    managed kernel service, or competing distribution — NO (Commons Clause).

The Commons Clause restriction targets cloud-provider extraction, not
application developers or SPI implementors. If you are uncertain whether your
use case is within scope, contact legal@exeris.eu before deployment.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TIER 2 — ENTERPRISE  (Exeris Commercial License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Modules:
  - exeris-kernel-enterprise

Licence file: LICENSE-ENTERPRISE (distributed with the Enterprise edition,
not at the root of this repository).
In the Enterprise distribution, the exeris-kernel-enterprise module carries a
copy of LICENSE-ENTERPRISE at its own module root.

Summary: evaluation use only without a signed commercial agreement.
Production use, SaaS/PaaS deployment, and redistribution require a separate
written licence. Contact legal@exeris.eu.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURAL NOTE FOR IMPLEMENTORS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The SPI module (exeris-kernel-spi) is the public contract surface. Any third
party may implement the SPI — including implementing QUIC, io_uring drivers,
or native transports — and distribute or sell those implementations under any
licence compatible with Apache 2.0 + Commons Clause dependency terms. The
Enterprise module is not required to use the SPI; it is one implementation of
it. Exeris's commercial moat is the integrated io_uring + native slab allocator
+ support SLA stack, not the SPI contract itself.

